Suppose each full Newton step begins in a fixed narrow neighborhood of the central path and reduces the barrier parameter according to \(\mu_{k+1}=(1-	heta/\sqrt{
u})\mu_k\), where \(	heta\in(0,1)\) is an absolute neighborhood-dependent constant. Then the iterates remain in that neighborhood and \(\mu_k\leq\varepsilon\) after \(O(\sqrt{
u}\log(\mu_0/\varepsilon))\) iterations. For the logarithmic-determinant barrier \(-\log\det X\) on \(\mathbb S_{++}^{n}\), the barrier parameter is \(
u=n\), giving \(O(\sqrt n\log(\mu_0/\varepsilon))\) iterations.
